e box whose edges are each marker moved one step toward the shape, and each marker ends up touching the frame from outside.\n\n**How to find the parts in general:**\n- The markers are the single-cell objects, which all share one colour.\n- The top marker has the smallest y, the bottom one the largest y, the left one the smallest x and the right one the largest x.\n- The frame colour is the colour of the remaining, larger object.\n\n**Construction stages:**\n1. Draw the top edge.\n2. Draw the bottom edge.\n3. Draw the left and right sides.\n\n**Test input:** the markers are at (1,7), (13,5), (6,2) and (9,12), and the shape is colour 8.\n- The frame spans rows 2–12 and columns 3–11.\n- It is drawn in colour 8 around the 8-shape at rows 5–7, columns 5–8.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    singles = [o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] == 1]\n    big = [o for o in objs if o[\"size\"] > 1]\n    col = max(big, key=lambda o: o[\"size\"])[\"colour\"]\n    pts = [o[\"cells\"][0] for o in singles]\n    top = min(p[0] for p in pts) + 1\n    bot = max(p[0] for p in pts) - 1\n    left = min(p[1] for p in pts) + 1\n    right = max(p[1] for p in pts) - 1\n    out = g.copy()\n    out[top, left:right + 1] = col\n    emit(out, \"Top edge of the frame: one row below the top marker, spanning between the left and right markers.\")\n    out[bot, left:right + 1] = col\n    emit(out, \"Bottom edge: one row above the bottom marker.\")\n    out[top:bot + 1, left] = col\n    out[top:bot + 1, right] = col\n    emit(out, \"Left and right sides: one column inside the left and right markers, closing the frame.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The top marker has the smallest y, the bottom one the largest y, the left one the smallest x and the right one the largest x."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifa